title: "Porous Thermal AI: applicability boundaries of physics, random forest and residual hybrid models"
authors:
  - name: "Forever61T"
    affiliation: "Independent course project; GitHub maintainer handle"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/Forever61T/porous-thermal-ai"
url: "https://github.com/Forever61T/porous-thermal-ai"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - porous materials
  - thermal conductivity
  - finite volume method
  - residual learning
  - model applicability
abstract: >-
  A frozen 2D numerical benchmark comparing effective-medium physics,
  random forests and additive physics-plus-ML residual correction across
  grouped in-distribution, held-out intermediate porosity, high-porosity
  extrapolation and unseen structural-family tests. Experimental aerogel
  prediction and universal hybrid superiority are not claimed.
